    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Conversion Factors\n\n- **1 Cubic Foot (CF)** ≈ 1,000 BTUs\n- **1 CFH** ≈ 1 MBH (MBH = thousands of BTUs per hour)\n- **1 MBH** = 1,000 BTU/h (0.29 kW)\n- **1 Btu/h** = 0.293 W\n- **1 psi** = 6,894.8 Pa (N/m²)\n- **1 in water** = 248.8 N/m² = 0.0361 psi = 25.4 kg/m²\n- **1 lb** = 0.4536 kg\n- **1 ft** = 0.3048 m\n\n## Notes\n\n- Inlet upstream pressure must be more than 5 psig (35 kPa)\n- Fittings factor 1.2 - equivalent pipe length = pipe length + 20%\n- Capacity tables are for Steel Pipes Schedule 40\n- Natural gas nominal BTU/cf varies from about 900 to 1100 BTU/cf"
